 "about": {
  "text": "West Wind stands on the coastal hills at Mākara, west of Wellington, where Cook Strait funnels strong, steady winds. Meridian began building it in 2007, bringing the turbine parts in through a temporary wharf at Oteranga Bay and 33 km of new roads to keep them off the city's streets. Its 62 turbines, up to 142.6 MW, were fully running in 2009, and a public recreation area lets visitors walk and bike among them.",
